 \"compute a quote from customer+items\" — it hasn't narrowed to something more specific (e.g., \"single item lookup\") that would demand a rename.\n\n**Decision: Keep current name `computeQuote`** — it fits the full intent seen so far.\n\n### Step 2: Initial APP Mass (changed region)\n\nBefore:\n```ts\nif (items.length === 0) {\n  return { premium: PROCESSING_FEE };\n}\nconst itemBasePremium = BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type];\n```\n- Bindings: `items` (x2), `itemBasePremium`, `PROCESSING_FEE` = 4\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n- Conditionals: `if` statement = 1 (mass 4)\n- Invocations: property/index lookups (`items[0].type`, `BASE_PREMIUMS[...]`) = 2 (mass 2 each) = 4\n- Early `return` adds a second exit point (structural cost, not directly in mass formula but relevant to Rule 4 — fewest elements/control-flow paths)\n\nMass ≈ (4×1) + (1×1) + (1×4) + (2×2) = 4 + 1 + 4 + 4 = **13**, plus a second function exit point.\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: 3/3 passing before change. ✅ baseline confirmed.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The early-return special-case for `items.length === 0` fragments the function into two exit paths, obscuring that \"no items\" is really just \"zero base premium\" flowing through the *same* calculation pipeline (surcharge, rounding, fee). Collapsing it into the existing arithmetic pipeline makes the single unified formula more visible.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: No duplication found — this is a Rule 2/4 issue, not DRY.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Removing the early `return` and dedicated `if` block reduces the function to a single control-flow path with one `return` statement.\n\n### Step 4: Implemented Refactoring\n\nReplaced the early-return guard clause with an inline conditional expression that folds the empty-list case into the same computation pipeline:\n\n```ts\nconst itemBasePremium =\n  items.length === 0 ? 0 : BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type];\n```\n\nRan `pnpm test` after the change — all 3 tests 