s Intent): The rounding expression `Math.round((x + fee) * PRECISION) / PRECISION` then `Math.ceil(...)` mixes two distinct concerns (float-noise correction and \"round up in the insurer's favor\" business rule) inline inside `computeQuote`, obscuring the top-level flow of: base premium → surcharge → fee → round. Extracting this into a named helper `roundUpInInsurersFavor` makes the main function read as a clear pipeline and gives a name to a business rule that the spec explicitly calls out (\"Rounding in MHPCO's favor\" — an upcoming test target), improving intent-revealing now and preparing for that test.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication present yet with only one item type.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Extracting a helper adds one function but removes one intermediate binding and clarifies structure — net neutral on element count, justified by Rule 2.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Extracted the rounding/float-noise logic into a dedicated `roundUpInInsurersFavor` helper function, so `computeQuote` reads as a clear sequence: look up base premium → apply first-insurance surcharge → round up (with fee) in insurer's favor.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const itemBasePremium =\n    items.length === 0 ? 0 : BASE_PREMIUMS[items[0].type];\n  const withFirstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    itemBasePremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(withFirstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { premium };\n};\n```\n\nComponent Count (combined, both functions):\n- Constants: `0` (empty list), `1` (surcharge base) = 2\n- Bindings: `customer`, `items`, `itemBasePremium`, `withFirstInsuranceSurcharge`, `premium`, `amount`, `roundedToAvoidFloatNoise` = 7\n- Invocations: `roundUpInInsurersFavor` call, `Math.round`, `Math.ceil` = 3 → mass 6\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary) = 4\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\nTotal Mass: 2 + 7 + 6 + 4 + 0 + 0 = **19**\n\n**Mass Change**: 15 → 19 (delta +4)\n\nMass increased slightly due to the extra function call and parameter binding introduced by the extraction. This is an accepted trade-off: Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) outranks APP mass. The extraction gives a name to the \"round up in insurer's favor\" business rule (directly relevant to an upcoming spec item) and declutters `computeQuote`'s main body into a readable top-to-bottom pipeline, at the cost of a small mass increase.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted rounding/float-noise logic into named helper `roundUpInInsurersFavor`, clarifying `computeQuote`'s pipeline structure. Naming of `computeQuote` itself was evaluated and kept as-is (fits its role as top-level public API).\n**Mass Change**: 15 → 19 (+4, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 4 tests passing (verified via `pnpm test`)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added a \"staff: 80\" entry to the BASE_PREMIUMS lookup map (no logic changes) so quotes for single staff items resolve their base premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: Added a \"staff: 80\" entry to the BASE_PREMIUMS lookup map (no logic chan