(`reduce`) = 5\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 17\n\n**Refactoring Applied** (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent):\nExtracted the ternary pricing rule into a named function `premiumForType(type, count)`, separating \"how is a single type priced\" from \"how are all types summed.\" Added a one-line comment explaining the block-discount rule, since the magic behavior (exact count match, not >=) is a business rule worth calling out explicitly.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst premiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nconst policyBasePremium = Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n  (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n  0\n);\n```\n- Constants: 1 = 1\n- Bindings: 4 (`type`, `count` params + `type`, `count`, `sum` in reduce) ≈ 4\n- Invocations: 3 (`Object.entries`, `.reduce`, `premiumForType`) = 6\n- Conditionals: 1 (moved into `premiumForType`) = 4\n- Loops: 1 = 5\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 20 (slightly higher — one extra invocation)\n\n**Mass Change**: 17 → 20 (+3)\n\n**Decision rationale**: Mass increased slightly due to the extra function-call indirection, but Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) outranks APP mass. Naming the pricing rule `premiumForType` makes the block-discount business logic independently readable and testable in isolation from the aggregation loop, and the accompanying comment documents the \"exactly BLOCK_SIZE\" semantics that will matter once the `it.todo` tests for 4 and 7 runes are activated (where the non-block case must be handled correctly). This is a worthwhile tradeoff of a few mass points for clarity that will pay off in the next Red cycles.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted ternary pricing rule into named `premiumForType` helper (Rule 2: Reveals Intent) + added explanatory comment on block-discount business rule\n**Mass Change**: 17 → 20 (+3, accepted for clarity per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 7 passing, no regressions"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added a countByType helper that groups items by type. computeQuote now computes the policy base premium by iterating counts: if a type's count equals exactly BLOCK_SIZE (3), it uses the special BLOCK_PREMIUM (60 G) instead of count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type]. Removed the now-unused basePremiumFor helper from the previous cycle.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 7\nRecent Green phase: Added a countByType helper that groups items by type. computeQuote now computes the policy base premium by iterating counts: if a type's count equals exactly BLOCK_SIZE (3), it uses the special BLOCK_PREMIUM (60 G) instead of count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type]. Removed the now-unused basePremiumFor helper from the previous cycle.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784914997152},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01RiFRBnpsn9A5pGPUE5PCZp","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01U3k9qDXBd9wVqpuVGFLtVu","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":279,"output":114,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10161,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914997171,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e1f6a248-194f-4d5e-a718-ffe3483117c4","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01RiFRBnpsn9A5pGPUE5PCZp","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n};\n\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst countByType = (items: QuoteItem[]): Record<string, number> =>\n  items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) =>\n      sum + (count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type]),\n    0\n  );\n  const withFirstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    policyBasePremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(withFirstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { premium };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914998735},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01U3k9qDXBd9wVqpuVGFLtVu","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeQuote } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote\", () => {\n  // --- Edge cases: simplest first ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, []);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (isolation) ---\n  it(\"single sword, no modifiers, first quote -> base 100 G + 10% first insurance = 110 + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet, no modifiers, first quote -> base 60 G + 10% first insurance = 66 + 5 fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff, no modifiers, first quote -> base 80 G + 10% first insurance = 88 + 5 fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"staff\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion, no modifiers, first quote -> base 40 G + 10% first insurance = 44 + 5 fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"potion\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (no block) -> final premium 60 G (50*1.1=55, +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies) -> final premium 71 G (60*1.1=66, +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block - requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G\");\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components: same type required for block ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy with cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) -> item-specific curse surcharge (50 G) applies only to cursed sword's base premium, policy base 160 G + 50 G curse = 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount (20%) applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge (30%) applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> both curse (50%) and high-enchantment (30%) surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 4 -> curse surcharge applies, no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n\n  // --- Rounding in MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> rounds up to 198 G\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3): 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 -> +5 fee = 165 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer's (3 years) second quote with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 7): \" +\n      \"100 base + 50 curse + 30 high-ench - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 -> +5 fee = 160 G \" +\n      \"(first insurance surcharge still applies per item, regardless of customer history)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Error case ---\n  it.todo(\"quote includes an item with unknown type (e.g. broomstick) -> throws/rejects with error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914998735},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01176VG39yrWFXeXeeVePc6