hen mixed).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":915,"output":366,"cacheRead":78145,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":79426,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784915470296,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6541b130-38cc-4610-96c8-92d1cbb4cf9d","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01YPq98rf69rNgKjcDWYoQgH","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 10 tests still pass.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (`computeQuote` + new `sumBasePremiums`):\n```ts\nconst sumBasePremiums = (counts: Record<string, number>): number =>\n  Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = sumBasePremiums(counts);\n  const withFirstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    policyBasePremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(withFirstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { premium };\n};\n```\n- `sumBasePremiums`: Bindings(counts, sum, type, count)=4, Invocations(Object.entries, .reduce, premiumForType)=3→6, Loop=1→5, Constant(0)=1 → **16**\n- `computeQuote`: Bindings(customer, items, counts, policyBasePremium, withFirstInsuranceSurcharge, premium)=6, Invocations(countByType, sumBasePremiums, roundUpInInsurersFavor)=3→6 → **12**\n\n**Total Mass: 16 + 12 = 28** (was 25, delta **+3**)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Naming**: Evaluated first — all existing names (`countByType`, `premiumForType`, `roundUpInInsurersFavor`, `computeQuote`) still accurately describe their behavior after the moonstone addition. No renames needed.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Extracted `sumBasePremiums(counts)` from the inline `Object.entries(...).reduce(...)` expression inside `computeQuote`. Previously `computeQuote` mixed a raw collection-pipeline expression with calls to named helpers for the other two pipeline stages (`countByType`, `roundUpInInsurersFavor`). Now all three stages read uniformly as named function calls, making `computeQuote`'s top-level body a flat, self-documenting composition: count → sum base premiums → apply surcharge → round.\n- **Mass**: Increased slightly (25 → 28, +3) because extracting a named function adds a small fixed overhead (one more invocation wrapper). This is an accepted tradeoff: **Rule 2 (clarity) trumps APP** when, as here, the mass increase is minor and intent is clearly improved.\n\n**Tests**: All 10 tests passing, no regressions."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added \"moonstone: 25\" to BASE_PREMIUMS map. This confirms that countByType/premiumForType logic already correctly treats runes and moonstones as separate types (no block discount when mixed).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added \"moonstone: 25\" to BASE_PREMIUMS map. This confirms that countByType/premiumForType logic already correctly treats runes and moonstones as separate types (no block discount when mixed).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784915475010},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019kmEktT92uHKi311LFaUuw","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017HCczcCMVMPmhNxadK3anQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":221,"output":257,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10246,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784915475029,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8d0ad121-29ab-4872-b578-aa850f6efb9b","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_019kmEktT92uHKi311LFaUuw","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst countByType = (items: QuoteItem[]): Record<string, number> =>\n  items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\n// A \"block\" of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced at a flat\n// BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of the usual per-item rate.\nconst premiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[]\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n  const withFirstInsuranceSurcharge =\n    policyBasePremium * (1 + FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(withFirstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n  return { premium };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915477361},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_017HCczcCMVMPmhNxadK3anQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeQuote } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Quote\", () => {\n  // --- Edge cases: simplest first ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, []);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (isolation) ---\n  it(\"single sword, no modifiers, first quote -> base 100 G + 10% first insurance = 110 + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet, no modifiers, first quote -> base 60 G + 10% first insurance = 66 + 5 fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff, no modifiers, first quote -> base 80 G + 10% first insurance = 88 + 5 fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"staff\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion, no modifiers, first quote -> base 40 G + 10% first insurance = 44 + 5 fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"potion\" }]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // --- Building block of 3 alike components ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> base premium 50 G (no block) -> final premium 60 G (50*1.1=55, +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> base premium 60 G (block applies) -> final premium 71 G (60*1.1=66, +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> base premium 100 G (no block, requires exactly 3) -> final premium 115 G (100*1.1=110, +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> base premium 175 G -> final premium 198 G (175*1.1=192.5, +5 fee=197.5, rounded up)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote(\n      { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }))\n    );\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(198);\n  });\n\n  // --- \"Alike\" components: same type required for block ---\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> base premium 75 G (no block: different types) -> final premium 88 G (75*1.1=82.5, +5=87.5, rounded up)\", () => {\n    const result = computeQuote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ]);\n    expect(result.premium).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> base premium 120 G (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy with cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) -> item-specific curse surcharge (50 G) applies only to cursed sword's base premium, policy base 160 G + 50 G curse = 210 G before further modifiers and fee\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO -> loyalty discount (20%) applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge (30%) applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> both curse (50%) and high-enchantment (30%) surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 4 -> curse surcharge applies, no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n\n  // --- Rounding in MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> rounds up to 198 G\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3): 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 -> +5 fee = 165 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer's (3 years) second quote with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 7): \" +\n      \"100 base + 50 curse + 30 high-ench - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 -> +5 fee = 160 G \" +\n      \"(first insurance surcharge still applies per item, regardless of customer history)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Error case ---\n  it.todo(\"quote includes an item with unknown type (e.g. broomstick) -> throws/rejects with error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915477361},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KfbzHa6mL1JTfB8wYTieb5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thi