ne `.reduce()` in `computeQuote` into a named `sumCurseSurcharges(items)` helper, mirroring the existing `sumBasePremiums(counts)` helper.\n- Naming: kept all existing names — they already fit their purpose precisely.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication / conceptual symmetry): both \"aggregate a per-item/per-type value\" operations now follow the same named-helper pattern instead of one being inline and the other extracted, making `computeQuote`'s body read as a flat, uniform pipeline of named steps.\n\n**Why mass went up slightly**: the extra function adds one more invocation (`+2`) and a binding for the parameter name repeated across two scopes, but per Rule 2 (clarity trumps APP), the gain in structural consistency and readability of `computeQuote` (now five clearly-named, symmetrical steps) outweighs the small mass increase. `computeQuote`'s own body mass actually dropped in complexity — it now reads purely as named-step composition with no inline reduce logic to parse.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted inline curse-surcharge reduce into named `sumCurseSurcharges` helper for structural symmetry with `sumBasePremiums`, improving readability of `computeQuote`'s pipeline (Rule 3/Rule 2).\n**Mass Change**: 32 -> 35 (+3, accepted per Rule 2 — clarity trumps APP for this small delta)\n**Tests**: All 12 passing, no regressions"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1116,"output":1103,"cacheRead":15321,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17540,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784915902042,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-37d9b8d4-6a38-48a4-89e8-45baeb16ccb8","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":29427,"output":6097,"cacheRead":55041,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":17540,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":178491591251