licyBasePremium);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(\n    policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      discount +\n      PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n  return { premium };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916335938},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Refactored Code Mass**\n\n```\ncurseSurchargeFor:\n  - Constants: 1 (0)\n  - Bindings: 1 (item)\n  - Invocations: 1 (basePremiumOf)\n  - Conditionals: 1\n  Mass = 1 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 8\n\nhighEnchantmentSurchargeFor:\n  - Constants: 2 (0 default, 0 fallback in comparison already counted once — count literal 0 twice: ?? 0 and : 0)\n  - Bindings: 1 (item)\n  - Invocations: 1 (basePremiumOf)\n  - Conditionals: 1\n  Mass = 2 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 9\n\nbasePremiumOf (new):\n  - Bindings: 1 (item)\n  - Invocations: 0 (property/index access, not a call)\n  Mass = 1\n\nsumItemSurcharges: unchanged\n  - Constants: 1 (0)\n  - Bindings: 2 (sum, item)\n  - Invocations: 3 (reduce, curseSurchargeFor, highEnchantmentSurchargeFor)\n  - Loops: 1 (reduce)\n  Mass = 1 + 2 + 6 + 5 = 14\n```\n\nTotal (four functions): 8 + 9 + 1 + 14 = **32** (down from 35)\n\n**Mass Change**: 35 → 32 (delta -3)\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `basePremiumOf(item)` helper to eliminate duplicated `BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type]` lookup, previously repeated identically in `curseSurchargeFor` and `highEnchantmentSurchargeFor` (Rule 3: No Duplication). This also strengthens Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) by giving the concept \"an item's own base premium\" an explicit name, matching how the Green-phase description already referred to it in prose.\n\n**Naming**: All existing names (`curseSurchargeFor`, `highEnchantmentSurchargeFor`, `sumItemSurcharges`, etc.) still accurately describe their behavior — no renames needed.\n\n**Mass Change**: 35 → 32 (delta -3)\n\n**Tests**: All 14 passing tests remain green (verified via `pnpm test`)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vert