re refactor):\n```ts\nconst curseSurchargeFor = (item) =>\n  item.cursed ? percentOf(CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item)) : 0;\nconst highEnchantmentSurchargeFor = (item) =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? percentOf(HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item)) : 0;\nconst loyaltyDiscount = (customer, policyBasePremium) =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS\n    ? percentOf(LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium) : 0;\nconst followUpDiscount = (previousQuoteCount, policyBasePremium) =>\n  previousQuoteCount > 0\n    ? percentOf(FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium) : 0;\n```\nComponent count: constants 4 (rates), bindings ~10 (params/consts referenced), invocations 8 (percentOf x4, basePremiumOf x2, plus comparisons), conditionals 4 (one ternary each) → mass ≈ 4×1 + 10×1 + 8×2 + 4×4 = 4+10+16+16 = **46**\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```ts\nconst percentIf = (condition, rate, base) => (condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0);\nconst curseSurchargeFor = (item) => percentIf(item.cursed, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item));\nconst highEnchantmentSurchargeFor = (item) =>\n  percentIf((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item));\nconst loyaltyDiscount = (customer, policyBasePremium) =>\n  percentIf(customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium);\nconst followUpDiscount = (previousQuoteCount, policyBasePremium) =>\n  percentIf(previousQuoteCount > 0, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium);\n```\nComponent count: constants 4, bindings ~11 (added `percentIf` params), invocations 9 (percentIf x4, percentOf x1 inside it, basePremiumOf x2, comparisons), conditionals 1 (only inside `percentIf` now) → mass ≈ 4 + 11 + 18 + 4 = **37**\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): The four discount/surcharge functions all shared the identical \"apply rate to base only if condition holds\" shape, duplicated as four separate ternaries. Extracted this into `percentIf(condition, rate, base)`.\n- Rule 2 preserved: each call site now reads as a one-line declarative rule (e.g. `percentIf(item.cursed, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item))`), arguably clearer than before since the \"conditional-rate\" pattern is named explicitly.\n- Mass reduced from 46 to 37 by collapsing four duplicated conditionals into one.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted duplicated conditional-percentage pattern into `percentIf` helper, used by `curseSurchargeFor`, `highEnchantmentSurchargeFor`, `loyaltyDiscount`, and `followUpDiscount`.\n**Mass Change**: 46 → 37 (reduced duplication)\n**Tests**: All 20 passing, no regressions."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":7596,"output":1593,"cacheRead":10081,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":19270,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784916935750,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c80e4a08-e39e-42b7-af55-3188dbb4f229","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":31546,"output":18546,"cacheRead":59547,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":19270,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916949101},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01TAuwFp3LH56MGHKFfaZKR1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && cat src/quote.ts && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3129,"output":142,"cacheRead":117893,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":121164,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916949106,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6500b25c-778f-4672-822a-f6a88f5c6642","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TAuwFp3LH56MGHKFfaZKR1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst countByType = (items: QuoteItem[]): Record<string, number> =>\n  items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\n// A \"block\" of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced at a flat\n// BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of the usual per-item rate.\nconst premiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (counts: Record<string, number>): number =>\n  Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\nconst basePremiumOf = (item: QuoteItem): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\n// Shared shape behind every surcharge/discount: a rate applied to a base amount.\nconst percentOf = (rate: number, base: number): number => rate * base;\n\n// Every surcharge/discount rule follows the same \"apply this rate to this\n// base, but only when some condition holds\" shape. Centralizing it here\n// means each rule below just states its condition and rate.\nconst percentIf = (condition: unknown, rate: number, base: number): number =>\n  condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0;\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst curseSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(item.cursed, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE, basePremiumOf(item));\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst highEnchantmentSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    basePremiumOf(item)\n  );\n\nconst sumItemSurcharges = (items: QuoteItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) =>\n      sum + curseSurchargeFor(item) + highEnchantmentSurchargeFor(item),\n    0\n  );\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscount = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst followUpDiscount = (\n  previousQuoteCount: number,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(previousQuoteCount > 0, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium);\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[],\n  previousQuoteCount = 0\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = sumBasePremiums(counts);\n  const itemSurcharges = sumItemSurcharges(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = percentOf(\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n  const discount = loyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  const followUp = followUpDiscount(previousQuoteCount, policyBasePremium);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(\n    policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      discount -\n      followUp +\n      PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n  return { premium };\n};\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (21 tests | 1 skipped) 4ms\n ↓ src/claim.spec.ts  (15 tests | 15 skipped)\n ↓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (8 tests | 8 skipped)\n\n Test Files  1 passed | 2 skipped (3)\n      Tests  20 passed | 24 todo (44)\n   Start at  18:15:52\n   Duration  394ms (transform 36ms, setup 0ms, collect 41ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 125ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784916952717},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I want to fix the `condition: unknown` type — let's use `boolean` for clarity/safety."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01YNPA9jRwxQqrngQrosfQeQ","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const percentIf = (condition: boolean, rate: number, base: number): number =>\n  condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0;","oldText":"const percentIf = (condition: unknown, rate: number, base: number): number =>\n  condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0;"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/src/quote.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4279,"output":286,"cacheRead":119093,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":123658,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784916952720,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2545ed25-a1ce-4e4d-a072-20213d5ac86f","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_