 Function purpose so far: \"given a list of damages, take the first damage amount and subtract a flat deductible, returning payout and updated remaining cap\"\n- Question: Does `computeClaim` reveal this intent?\n- Assessment: Yes — the name is appropriately generic for a public API that will grow to handle policy matching, multiple damages, and cap logic (per the test list). It should **not** be narrowed to something like `applyDeductibleToFirstDamage`, since that would describe today's stub implementation rather than the claim-computation contract the tests are building toward.\n- Decision: **Keep `computeClaim`** — name still fits; premature narrowing would fight the upcoming tests (multiple damages, per-item deductibles, cap exhaustion, etc.).\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before refactor):\n```ts\nconst payout = damages[0].amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\nreturn { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n```\n- Constants: 1 (`0` index literal) = 1\n- Bindings: `damages`, `DEDUCTIBLE`, `payout` (decl), `remainingCap`, `payout` (reuse) = 5\n- Invocations: 0\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 1 (`const payout = ...`) x6 = 6\n\nTotal Mass: 1 + 5 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 6 = **12**\n\n**Simple Design Rules applied**:\n- Rule 1 (Tests Pass): 22/22 passing before and after — never at risk.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): The bare expression `damages[0].amount - DEDUCTIBLE` buries the domain concept \"the deductible is subtracted from the raw damage amount\" inside an anonymous arithmetic line. Extracted a named helper `applyDeductible(amount)` so the subtraction reads as a domain operation, matching the small-named-helper style already established in `quote.ts` (`percentOf`, `percentIf`, `basePremiumOf`, etc.), which this codebase clearly favors for consistency.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication present yet at this stage.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Considered leaving it inline since there's only one call site — but Rule 2 (clarity, and consistency with the project's established idiom) took priority over the minor mass increase.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (after refactor):\n```ts\nconst applyDeductible = (amount: number): number => amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n\nconst payout = applyDeductible(damages[0].amount);\nreturn { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n```\n- Constants: 1 (`0` index) = 1\n- Bindings: `amount` (param), `DEDUCTIBLE`, `damages`, `payout` (decl), `remainingCap`, `payout` (reuse) = 6\n- Invocations: 1 (`applyDeductible(...)`) x2 = 2\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 1 (`const payout = ...`) x6 = 6\n\nTotal Mass: 1 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 0 + 6 = **15**\n\n**Mass Change**: 12 -> 15 (delta +3)\n\n**Decision rationale**: Mass increased slightly, but Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP per the guidelines. Naming the deductible step aligns `claim.ts` with the readable, small-function idiom already established in `quote.ts`, which will make it easier to extend this file consistently as later tests introduce per-item deductibles, caps, and multiple damages.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `applyDeductible` helper to name the deductible-subtraction step; kept `computeClaim` name unchanged (still fits intent).\n**Mass Change**: 12 -> 15 (+3, accepted for clarity per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 22 passing (1 active in claim.spec.ts, rest todo/skipped as expected)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 1 (in claim.spec.ts; 22 total across project)\nRecent Green phase: computeClaim(policyItems, damages, remainingCap) now reads damages[0].amount, subtracts a flat DEDUCTIBLE (100), and returns { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout }. It ignores policyItems and only handles a single damage entry.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 1 (in claim.spec.ts; 22 total across project)\nRecent Green phase: computeClaim(policyItems, damages, remainingCap) now reads damages[0].amount, subtracts a flat DEDUCTIBLE (100), and returns { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout }. It ignores policyItems and only handles a single damage entry.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784917111631},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01MbuUbXaxnG9aNeTaX4gYNh","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01XH9CUJUuteymwDiJttBj69","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":265,"output":116,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10149,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784917111651,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ed0511df-65b7-45ae-86ff-f4cc03a952da","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MbuUbXaxnG9aNeTaX4gYNh","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { QuoteItem } from \"./quote.js\";\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  remainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const payout = damages[0].amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784917113381},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01XH9CUJUuteymwDiJttBj69","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaim } from \"./claim.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim\", () => {\n  // --- Standard reimbursement (no special clauses), simplest first ---\n  it(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it.todo(\n    \"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus deductible; no enchantment/material)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon attack damages insured sword (500 G) and insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (50% rule wins over full reimbursement, then deductible: 500-100)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800-100)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible: 500-100)\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies at threshold, then deductible)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"policy covers two swords, dragon attack damages both (two separate damage entries of itemType sword) -> each treated as separate damage with its own deductible\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"damages array contains more entries of a given type than policy covers (e.g. two sword damages but only one sword insured) -> rejected with error\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first payout 1400 G, remaining cap 600 G\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\n    \"second successive 1500 G claim after first claim's cap reduction -> payout 600 G, remaining cap 0 G (desired 1400 G reduced to remaining cap)\"\n  );\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it.todo(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> rounds down to 350 G\");\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy (e.g. amulet damaged when only sword insured) -> rejected with error\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\"claim references a damage entry with unknown item type -> rejected with error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200 -> rejected with error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784917113381},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SJWN8gj9C3qkY8TW3h7rCR","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat src/quote.ts 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; cat package.json; echo \"---\"; cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1734,"output":616,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12118,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784917113381,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d3e77940-0692-4f04-9c9a-9a76ec4470b0","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01SJWN8gj9C3qkY8TW3h7rCR","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst basePremiumOf = (type: string): number => {\n  const premium = BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n  if (premium === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return premium;\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: QuoteItem[]): Record<string, number> =>\n  items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\n// A \"block\" of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced at a flat\n// BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of the usual per-item rate.\nconst premiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * basePremiumOf(type);\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (counts: Record<string, number>): number =>\n  Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\n// Shared shape behind every surcharge/discount: a rate applied to a base amount.\nconst percentOf = (rate: number, base: number): number => rate * base;\n\n// Every surcharge/discount rule follows the same \"apply this rate to this\n// base, but only when some condition holds\" shape. Centralizing it here\n// means each rule below just states its condition and rate.\nconst percentIf = (condition: boolean, rate: number, base: number): number =>\n  condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0;\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst curseSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    item.cursed ?? false,\n    CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    basePremiumOf(item.type)\n  );\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst highEnchantmentSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    basePremiumOf(item.type)\n  );\n\nconst sumItemSurcharges = (items: QuoteItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) =>\n      sum + curseSurchargeFor(item) + highEnchantmentSurchargeFor(item),\n    0\n  );\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscount = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst followUpDiscount = (\n  previousQuoteCount: number,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(previousQuoteCount > 0, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium);\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[],\n  previousQuoteCount = 0\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = sumBasePremiums(counts);\n  const itemSurcharges = sumItemSurcharges(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = percentOf(\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n  const discount = loyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  const followUp = followUpDiscount(previousQuoteCount, policyBasePremium);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(\n    policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      discount -\n      followUp +\n      PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n  return { premium };\n};\n---\n{\n  \"name\": \"tdd-experiment-run\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:unit:basic\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:watch\": \"vitest\",\n    \"test:coverage\": \"vitest run --coverage --coverage.reporter=json-summary\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"tsx\": \"^4.7.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"@vitest/coverage-v8\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^9.0.0\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-sonarjs\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"pnpm\": {\n    \"onlyBuiltDependencies\": [\"esbuild\"]\n  }\n}\n---\n\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (21 tests) 4ms\n ✓ src/claim.spec.ts  (15 tests | 14 skipped) 1ms\n ↓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (8 tests | 8 skipped)\n\n Test Files  2 passed | 1 skipped (3)\n      Tests  22 passed | 22 todo (44)\n   Start at  18:18:41\n   Duration  396ms (transform 37ms, setup 0ms, collect 44ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 123ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784917121723},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01RY2oi3GzsHn5uo38dqPEFU","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  remainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const payout = damages[0].amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};","newText":"const DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\n// Names the single arithmetic step the claim payout depends on today,\n// mirroring the small-named-helper style us