reimbursed amount, before the deductible is applied) that matters for reading the domain logic correctly.\n\n**Before:**\n```ts\nconst payoutFor = (policyItems: QuoteItem[], damage: Damage): number => {\n  const item = findPolicyItem(policyItems, damage.itemType);\n  const rate = reimbursementRateFor(item);\n  return applyDeductible(damage.amount * rate);\n};\n```\n\n**After:**\n```ts\nconst payoutFor = (policyItems: QuoteItem[], damage: Damage): number => {\n  const item = findPolicyItem(policyItems, damage.itemType);\n  const rate = reimbursementRateFor(item);\n  const reimbursedAmount = damage.amount * rate;\n  return applyDeductible(reimbursedAmount);\n};\n```\n\n### Step 4: APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Before:**\n- Bindings: `policyItems`, `damage`, `item`, `rate` = 4 × 1 = 4\n- Invocations: `findPolicyItem`, `reimbursementRateFor`, `*`, `applyDeductible` = 4 × 2 = 8\n- Total Mass: **12**\n\n**After:**\n- Bindings: `policyItems`, `damage`, `item`, `rate`, `reimbursedAmount` = 5 × 1 = 5\n- Invocations: `findPolicyItem`, `reimbursementRateFor`, `*`, `applyDeductible` = 4 × 2 = 8\n- Total Mass: **13**\n\n**Mass Change: 12 → 13 (delta +1)**\n\n### Step 5: Decision Rationale\n\nRule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP mass. The extra binding (+1 mass) buys a named intermediate value — `reimbursedAmount` — that makes explicit the two-stage nature of the payout calculation (reimburse, then deduct), which will matter increasingly as more clauses (e.g., dragon-material full reimbursement) are layered in. This is a deliberate, small trade of mass for clarity.\n\n### Step 6: Tests"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01EkXPu4RHmRAjjprctch2PC","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":840,"output":2475,"cacheRead":16064,