ms round UP.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1273,"output":502,"cacheRead":176042,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":177817,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918202955,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bcca8f14-b846-4a94-bab9-fe3f97a6e693","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MjtWuFUweEXxdxXu77pVsN","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 33 tests still pass. ✅\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (per file, now):\n```ts\n// claim.ts / quote.ts each contain:\nconst roundDownInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.floor(avoidFloatNoise(amount));\n```\n- Constants: 0 = 0\n- Bindings: `roundDownInInsurersFavor`(decl), `amount`(param+ref) = 2\n- Invocations: `Math.floor`, `avoidFloatNoise` = 2 × 2 = 4\n- Total per file: **6**\n\nShared module (`rounding.ts`, counted once):\n```ts\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\nexport const avoidFloatNoise = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n```\n- Constants: 1 (`1e6`) = 1\n- Bindings: `FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION`(decl+2 refs), `avoidFloatNoise`(decl), `amount`(param+ref) = 6\n- Invocations: `Math.round` = 1 × 2 = 2\n- Total: **9**\n\n**Mass Change**: previously duplicated 13 + 13 = 26 (two full copies) → now 6 + 6 + 9 (shared) = **21**\nDelta: **-5**, and the float-noise-correction knowledge now has a single representation instead of two independent copies that could drift apart.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Kept `roundDownInInsurersFavor` / `roundUpInInsurersFavor` — already reveal intent clearly; extracted helper named `avoidFloatNoise` for the shared step, matching the existing internal variable name.\n- Rule 3 (DRY): Extracted the duplicated float-noise-correction formula (`FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION`, `Math.round(amount * P) / P`) from `claim.ts` and `quote.ts` into a new shared `src/rounding.ts` module.\n- Kept the directional wrappers (`floor` vs `ceil`) separate per Rule 2 — merging them into one parameterized \"round\" function would obscure the domain-meaningful distinction (payouts round down for the insurer, premiums round up for the insurer), so clarity was prioritized over squeezing out a few more mass units.\n- Mass: 26 → 21 (duplicated knowledge eliminated; single source of truth for the rounding-precision constant and formula).\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted shared `avoidFloatNoise` helper into new `src/rounding.ts`, removing duplication between `claim.ts` and `quote.ts`'s rounding helpers.\n**Mass Change**: 26 -> 21 (delta -5)\n**Tests**: All 33 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 12 in claim.spec.ts (33 total)\nRecent Green phase: Added a roundDownInInsurersFavor(amount) helper that corrects for floating-point noise then applies Math.floor. computeClaim now wraps the cap-limited payout with this rounding before returning it. This mirrors roundUpInInsurersFavor in quote.ts (which uses Math.ceil for premiums), since payouts round DOWN in the insurer's favor while premiums round UP.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 12 in claim.spec.ts (33 total)\nRecent Green phase: Added a roundDownInInsurersFavor(amount) helper that corrects for floating-point noise then applies Math.floor. computeClaim now wraps the cap-limited payout with this rounding before returning it. This mirrors roundUpInInsurersFavor in quote.ts (which uses Math.ceil for premiums), since payouts round DOWN in the insurer's favor while premiums round UP.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784918209788},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_013tkG7Y9jMxGGsjDZqBfQ1w","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AiuEbPSW375ipvxqfcV6B1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":299,"output":118,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10185,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918209808,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b896f99e-e118-4b11-83f7-8252df03d04e","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_013tkG7Y9jMxGGsjDZqBfQ1w","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { QuoteItem, countByType } from \"./quote.js\";\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\n// Names the single arithmetic step the claim payout depends on today,\n// mirroring the small-named-helper style used throughout quote.ts.\nconst applyDeductible = (amount: number): number => amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 1;\n\nconst findPolicyItem = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  itemType: string\n): QuoteItem | undefined =>\n  policyItems.find((item) => item.type === itemType);\n\nconst reimbursementRateFor = (item: QuoteItem | undefined): number =>\n  (item?.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n    ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE\n    : FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n\nconst payoutFor = (policyItems: QuoteItem[], damage: Damage): number => {\n  const item = findPolicyItem(policyItems, damage.itemType);\n  const rate = reimbursementRateFor(item);\n  const reimbursedAmount = damage.amount * rate;\n  return applyDeductible(reimbursedAmount);\n};\n\nconst sumDeductedPayouts = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  damages: Damage[]\n): number =>\n  damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + payoutFor(policyItems, damage), 0);\n\nconst validateDamagesFitPolicy = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  damages: Damage[]\n): void => {\n  const insuredCounts = countByType(policyItems);\n  const damageCounts = countByType(\n    damages.map((damage) => ({ type: damage.itemType }))\n  );\n  for (const [itemType, count] of Object.entries(damageCounts)) {\n    if (count > (insuredCounts[itemType] ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(\n        `More damage entries for '${itemType}' than the policy covers`\n      );\n    }\n  }\n};\n\n// Names the domain rule that a claim's payout can never exceed what's\n// left of the policy's insurance cap, mirroring the small-named-helper\n// style used for applyDeductible above.\nconst capPayoutAtRemainingLimit = (\n  desiredPayout: number,\n  remainingCap: number\n): number => Math.min(desiredPayout, remainingCap);\n\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst roundDownInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.floor(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: QuoteItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  remainingCap: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  validateDamagesFitPolicy(policyItems, damages);\n  const desiredPayout = sumDeductedPayouts(policyItems, damages);\n  const payout = roundDownInInsurersFavor(\n    capPayoutAtRemainingLimit(desiredPayout, remainingCap)\n  );\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918211522},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01AiuEbPSW375ipvxqfcV6B1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaim } from \"./claim.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim\", () => {\n  // --- Standard reimbursement (no special clauses), simplest first ---\n  it(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -> payout 100 G (full reimbursement minus deductible; no enchantment/material)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"rune\" }],\n      [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n      500\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(100);\n  });\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it(\"dragon attack damages insured sword (500 G) and insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }],\n      [\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n      ],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n\n  // --- Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material ---\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (50% rule wins over full reimbursement, then deductible: 500-100)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800-100)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(700);\n  });\n  it(\"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible: 500-100)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies at threshold, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  // --- Multiple items of the same type ---\n  it(\"policy covers two swords, dragon attack damages both (two separate damage entries of itemType sword) -> each treated as separate damage with its own deductible\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }],\n      [\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 },\n      ],\n      4000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n  it(\"damages array contains more entries of a given type than policy covers (e.g. two sword damages but only one sword insured) -> rejected with error\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      computeClaim(\n        [{ type: \"sword\" }],\n        [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 300 },\n        ],\n        2000\n      )\n    ).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  // --- Cap exhaustion ---\n  it(\"sword insured (insurance sum 1000 G, cap 2000 G); two successive claims of 1500 G each -> first payout 1400 G, remaining cap 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\" }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(1400);\n    expect(result.remainingCap).toBe(600);\n  });\n  it(\"second successive 1500 G claim after first claim's cap reduction -> payout 600 G, remaining cap 0 G (desired 1400 G reduced to remaining cap)\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\" }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }],\n      600\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n    expect(result.remainingCap).toBe(0);\n  });\n\n  // --- Rounding in the MHPCO's favor ---\n  it(\"payout calculation yielding 350.5 G -> rounds down to 350 G\", () => {\n    const result = computeClaim(\n      [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 9 }],\n      [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }],\n      2000\n    );\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(350);\n  });\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\n    \"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy (e.g. amulet damaged when only sword insured) -> rejected with error\"\n  );\n  it.todo(\"claim references a damage entry with unknown item type -> rejected with error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim contains a damage entry with amount: -200 -> rejected with error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918211522},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018ndUiRXmnHzHteNtHNLGXB","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -60"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014b6CdnCYd1bs2kCz5D5h1T","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/quote.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3480,"output":207,"cacheRead":10065,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13752,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784918211523,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-802a1499-dacb-4dca-95a7-2441fbc53e83","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_018ndUiRXmnHzHteNtHNLGXB","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (21 tests) 4ms\n ✓ src/claim.spec.ts  (15 tests | 3 skipped) 3ms\n ↓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (8 tests | 8 skipped)\n\n Test Files  2 passed | 1 skipped (3)\n      Tests  33 passed | 11 todo (44)\n   Start at  18:36:55\n   Duration  417ms (transform 44ms, setup 0ms, collect 51ms, tests 7ms, environment 0ms, prepare 131ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918215509},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014b6CdnCYd1bs2kCz5D5h1T","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface QuoteItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst roundUpInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.ceil(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst basePremiumOf = (type: string): number => {\n  const premium = BASE_PREMIUMS[type];\n  if (premium === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return premium;\n};\n\nexport const countByType = (items: QuoteItem[]): Record<string, number> =>\n  items.reduce((counts, item) => {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    return counts;\n  }, {} as Record<string, number>);\n\n// A \"block\" of exactly BLOCK_SIZE alike items is priced at a flat\n// BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of the usual per-item rate.\nconst premiumForType = (type: string, count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * basePremiumOf(type);\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (counts: Record<string, number>): number =>\n  Object.entries(counts).reduce(\n    (sum, [type, count]) => sum + premiumForType(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n\n// Shared shape behind every surcharge/discount: a rate applied to a base amount.\nconst percentOf = (rate: number, base: number): number => rate * base;\n\n// Every surcharge/discount rule follows the same \"apply this rate to this\n// base, but only when some condition holds\" shape. Centralizing it here\n// means each rule below just states its condition and rate.\nconst percentIf = (condition: boolean, rate: number, base: number): number =>\n  condition ? percentOf(rate, base) : 0;\n\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst curseSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    item.cursed ?? false,\n    CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    basePremiumOf(item.type)\n  );\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst highEnchantmentSurchargeFor = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    basePremiumOf(item.type)\n  );\n\nconst sumItemSurcharges = (items: QuoteItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) =>\n      sum + curseSurchargeFor(item) + highEnchantmentSurchargeFor(item),\n    0\n  );\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscount = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst followUpDiscount = (\n  previousQuoteCount: number,\n  policyBasePremium: number\n): number =>\n  percentIf(previousQuoteCount > 0, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, policyBasePremium);\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: QuoteItem[],\n  previousQuoteCount = 0\n): QuoteResult => {\n  const counts = countByType(items);\n  const policyBasePremium = sumBasePremiums(counts);\n  const itemSurcharges = sumItemSurcharges(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = percentOf(\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE,\n    policyBasePremium\n  );\n  const discount = loyaltyDiscount(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  const followUp = followUpDiscount(previousQuoteCount, policyBasePremium);\n  const premium = roundUpInInsurersFavor(\n    policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      discount -\n      followUp +\n      PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n  return { premium };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918215509},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `roundDownInInsurersFavor`\n- Function purpose: corrects floating-point noise, then rounds an amount down (floor)\n- Question: Does the name reveal this intent, given all 12 passing tests including the new rounding test (`350.5 -> 350`)?\n- Assessment: Yes — it clearly signals \"round down\" and \"in insurer's favor,\" matching its sibling `roundUpInInsurersFavor` in `quote.ts`. The float-noise correction is an internal implementation detail already documented by the local variable name `roundedToAvoidFloatNoise`.\n\nDecision: **Keep current name** — it fits the current intent.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (the duplicated rounding logic, counted once per file):\n```\nconst FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION = 1e6;\nconst roundDownInInsurersFavor = (amount: number): number => {\n  const roundedToAvoidFloatNoise =\n    Math.round(amount * FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION) / FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION;\n  return Math.floor(roundedToAvoidFloatNoise);\n};\n```\n- Constants: 1 (`1e6`) = 1\n- Bindings: `FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION`(decl), `roundDownInInsurersFavor`(decl), `amount`(param+ref), `roundedToAvoidFloatNoise`(decl+ref), `FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION`(2 refs) = 8\n- Invocations: `Math.round`, `Math.floor` = 2 × 2 = 4\n- Total per file: **13**\n\nThis exact structure (only `Math.ceil` vs `Math.floor`, different name) is duplicated verbatim in `quote.ts`'s `roundUpInInsurersFavor`. **Total duplicated mass across the codebase: 13 + 13 = 26.**\n\nNow applying the Simple Design Rules in order:\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: All 33 tests currently pass. ✅ baseline confirmed.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Names are already clear (see naming evaluation above). No change needed here.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Found it — the \"correct for float noise, then round in a given direction\" logic (including the `FLOAT_NOISE_PRECISION` constant and formula) is knowledge duplicated identically across `claim.ts` and `quote.ts`. This is the refactoring target.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: N/A once duplication is resolved.\n\nI'll extract the shared float-noise-correction step into a new module, keeping the direction-specific (`floor` vs `ceil`) wrappers separate and clearly named in each file — merging them into one parameterized function would hurt clarity (Rule 2 trumps DRY/APP), since the direction is meaningfully different domain knowledge (payouts round down for the insurer, premiums round up for the insur