sults };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918640173},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Report\n\n**Naming Evaluation** (First Priority):\n- Function: `runScenario` — clearly orchestrates a customer + steps array into results. Fits its purpose; no rename needed.\n- Anonymous inline logic for cap derivation lacked a name: it computed `insuranceSum` via `.reduce` inline, then multiplied by `CAP_MULTIPLIER`, all inside the `\"quote\"` branch. This buried a named domain concept (\"a policy's cap is 2x its insurance value\") inside orchestration code.\n- Decision: Extract `insuranceSumOf` and `capFor` as named helpers, mirroring the established small-named-helper style already used in `quote.ts` (`basePremiumOf`, `percentOf`) and `claim.ts` (`capPayoutAtRemainingLimit`, `applyDeductible`). This keeps `runScenario` reading as pure orchestration and gives the cap-derivation rule a name and a single place to live.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (quote branch, before):\n```ts\nconst insuranceSum = step.items.reduce(\n  (sum, item) => sum + INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type],\n  0\n);\npolicies.push({\n  items: step.items,\n  remainingCap: insuranceSum * CAP_MULTIPLIER,\n});\n```\n- Bindings: `insuranceSum`, `sum`, `item` = 3\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n- Invocations: `.reduce`, `+`, `push`, `*` = 4 → mass 8\n- Loops: `.reduce` = 1 → mass 5\n- Assignments: 0\nTotal: 3 + 1 + 8 + 5 = 17\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (quote branch, after):\n```ts\nconst insuranceSumOf = (items) => items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type], 0);\nconst capFor = (items) => insuranceSumOf(items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n...\npolicies.push({ items: step.items, remainingCap: capFor(step.items) });\n```\nCall-site mass (what `runScenario` itself now carries):\n- Bindings: `step.items` reused (0 new) = 0\n- Invocations: `capFor()`, `push()` = 2 → mass 4\n- Loops/assignments: 0\nCall-site total: 4 (helper definitions are one-time fixed cost, reused across all quote steps)\n\n**Mass Change**: 17 (inline, per quote-branch execution) → 4 (call-site) + fixed helper cost, amortized across every future test that exercises the quote branch. Net effect: lower recurring mass inside `runScenario`, same total logic moved to reusable, named locations.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): `insuranceSumOf` and `capFor` name the domain concept \"cap = 2x insurance value\" that was previously anonymous inline arithmetic — matches the naming convention already established in sibling files.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication existed yet (single quote branch), but extraction pre-empts the module drifting from the codebase's helper-function convention.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Two small pure functions added — justified because they name a real domain rule referenced by the spec's `it.todo` tests (e.g., \"insurance sum 1600 G... cap 3200 G\"), not speculative abstraction.\n\n**Tests**: All 37 passing (7 todo unchanged)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":9633,"output":1189,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":20590,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784918640174,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e0fe7e66-e639-47a5-a348-30f1b5b3524e","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":56774,"output":17157,"cacheRead":70441,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":20590,"turns":8},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784918652877},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Ar9er6ifvUWcBZVisTdXCe","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_17-26-10_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && cat src/scenario.ts && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":